.policy "ruff-ruf022-unsorted-dunder-all" revision 3
.description "Keep the names in __all__ sorted: SCREAMING_CASE constants first, then CamelCase classes, then everything else, each group in natural order."
.language python
.mode steer
.scope include "**/*"

// Ruff RUF022: a module's `__all__` list or tuple of strings that is not in isort order: SCREAMING_CASE
// constants, then CamelCase classes, then the rest, each in natural order (digit runs by number). Checked:
// `__all__ = …` (one target), `__all__: T = …`, `__all__ += …` and `__all__.extend(…)` at module level (in an
// `if` too), when every element is a string and there are two or more. Reported at the sequence.
//   __all__ = ["b", "a"]                ← RUF022
//   __all__ = ["APRIL", "Day", "f"]     not reported
//   __all__ = ["a01", "a1"]             not reported: a run starting with 0 compares digit by digit
//   __all__ = {"b", "a"}                not reported: a set has no order
#include "python/ruff-sorting.rr"

.violation RUF022(at: node) code "RUF022"
    "Sort `__all__`: SCREAMING_CASE constants first, then CamelCase classes, then the rest, each in natural order (digit runs by number). Leave it if other code relies on the current order."
    suppress ruff "RUF022"
RUF022(m) :- all_seq(v), unsorted(v, "isort"), unparen(v, m).

sort_ask(v, "isort") :- all_seq(v).
